[38;2;124;124;124mTherefore $a/b = 1$, $a = b$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually we need to be careful: the order argument requires $u$ to have finite [0m
[38;2;124;124;124morder, which it does since $u^m = 1$. The order divides both $m$ and $n$, hence [0m[38;2;124;124;124mdivides $\gcd(m,n) = 1$, so order = 1, $u = 1$.[0m

